    {
      "id": "BSreLC-87gBHsOO5HdV6A",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3398.6087426985664,
      "y": 4384.284053230486,
      "width": 1434.635498046875,
      "height": 1120,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBu",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 395291303,
      "version": 36,
      "versionNonce": 20908325,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784471752081,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Simple Blog Publishing Process\n\n1. Choose a topic:\n   Select one clear topic that your target audience wants to learn about.\n\n2. Do basic research:\n   Collect accurate information, examples, screenshots, statistics, or code related to the topic.\n\n3. Create an outline:\n   Plan the blog sections, such as introduction, main points, step-by-step guide, and conclusion.\n\n4. Write the blog:\n   Explain the topic clearly using short paragraphs, headings, examples, and simple language.\n\n5. Edit and improve:\n   Check grammar, remove repeated information, verify facts, and make sure every step is understandable.\n\n6. Add images:\n   Include a featured image, screenshots, blog title, keywords, URL, and a short meta description.\n\n7. Choose a publishing platform:\n   Publish on platforms such as WordPress, Medium, Hashnode, Dev.to, Blogger, or your own website.\n\n8. Preview and publish:\n   Check how the blog looks on desktop and mobile, test links, and then publish it.\n\n9. Promote the blog:\n   Share it on Facebook, LinkedIn, YouTube, email, and relevant communities.\n\n10. Update it later:\n    Correct errors and update information when tools, software, or industry details change.\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Simple Blog Publishing Process\n\n1. Choose a topic:\n   Select one clear topic that your target audience wants to learn about.\n\n2. Do basic research:\n   Collect accurate information, examples, screenshots, statistics, or code related to the topic.\n\n3. Create an outline:\n   Plan the blog sections, such as introduction, main points, step-by-step guide, and conclusion.\n\n4. Write the blog:\n   Explain the topic clearly using short paragraphs, headings, examples, and simple language.\n\n5. Edit and improve:\n   Check grammar, remove repeated information, verify facts, and make sure every step is understandable.\n\n6. Add images:\n   Include a featured image, screenshots, blog title, keywords, URL, and a short meta description.\n\n7. Choose a publishing platform:\n   Publish on platforms such as WordPress, Medium, Hashnode, Dev.to, Blogger, or your own website.\n\n8. Preview and publish:\n   Check how the blog looks on desktop and mobile, test links, and then publish it.\n\n9. Promote the blog:\n   Share it on Facebook, LinkedIn, YouTube, email, and relevant communities.\n\n10. Update it later:\n    Correct errors and update information when tools, software, or industry details change.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
